## Report
Crash attempt: built and ran the wait-path unit test `cargo test -p storage with_bucket_write_snapshot_waits_for_temporary_drain_then_succeeds -- --nocapture`; it completed without hang ("test node::tests::with_bucket_write_snapshot_waits_for_temporary_drain_then_succeeds ... ok"). Valgrind and gdb attempts failed because the tools are not installed (`valgrind: command not found`, `gdb: command not found`). Code inspection shows the generation mutex is acquired while the PgStore guard is still held, and only then is the PgStore guard dropped before waiting: `begin_bucket_write_drain` (crates/storage/src/node/bucket_ops.rs:60-96) and `with_bucket_write_reservation_snapshot` (crates/storage/src/node/bucket_ops.rs:421-454). State changes that would notify (release reservation/end drain) must acquire the same PgStore lock before calling `notify_bucket_coordination_change` (crates/storage/src/node/bucket_ops.rs:590-610), and notify increments the generation under the same mutex (crates/storage/src/node.rs:427-432). This lock ordering prevents a state change/notification from occurring before the waiter samples the generation, so the missed-notification race described in the finding is not reachable in these paths.

